# UX workflow: move several Clips as one spatial selection.
# Purpose: proves NAV toggles occupied cells into one selection, held NAV moves
# its anchor across compatible Track columns, and one validation preserves the
# complete selection geometry.
# Expect: capture_changed:first_selected=launcher_ready
# Expect: capture_changed:multi_selected=first_selected
# Expect: capture_changed:group_target=multi_selected
# Expect: capture_changed:group_moved=group_target
# Expect: semantic:first_selected:effect=enter_clip_selection, semantic:first_selected:projection=selected
# Expect: semantic:multi_selected:effect=toggle_clip_selection, semantic:multi_selected:projection=selected
# Expect: semantic:group_target:effect=focus_launcher_row, semantic:group_target:projection=move_destination
# Expect: semantic:group_moved:effect=move_clip, semantic:group_moved:outcome=applied

0 scenario clip-launcher
100 capture screen launcher_ready

# Scene rail -> first occupied Clip, then select it. This focused fixture keeps
# the final compatible Track empty for an unambiguous horizontal group move.
300 encoder NAV 0.01
540 button NAV down
1600 tick
1680 capture screen first_selected
1760 button NAV up

# Move to the next row and toggle its occupied Clip into the selection.
1920 encoder OPT 0.01
2080 tap NAV 60
2320 capture screen multi_selected

# Start group placement at the anchor, cross two compatible Tracks, then move
# two rows down. Every enabled Track owns a resident Clip in row one; the
# combined X/Y translation therefore lands on two genuinely empty cells.
2400 tap LEFT_CENTER 60
2640 encoder NAV 0.01
2720 encoder NAV 0.01
2880 encoder OPT 0.01
2960 encoder OPT 0.01
3200 capture screen group_target
3280 tap BOTTOM_RIGHT 60
3540 capture screen group_moved
